      {
         "id": "SECTION_schyoty",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The Schyoty (счёты)\n\nWhen looking at the Schyoty (счёты) in **Figure 1**, we can observe that it is represented vertically. However, as Jessica Amarteifio shows in her work, it is also possible to use it horizontally (<htcite0>).\n\nAnother point we should highlight when comparing the (счёты) with the previous abacuses is the fact that there is no bar in it where, when moving a marker closer, it comes to represent a certain value. Nor are there markers with value 5. All markers have the same value 1. As a consequence of these differences, to represent a value on the abacus, we must position all markers on one side of the rod and represent a number by moving the necessary markers to the opposite side (<htcite1>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "957755a4-793d-46d1-b3f8-bd3ea721415d",
                     "text": "Amarteifio, Jessica",
                     "page": "pp. 4 - 9",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "957755a4-793d-46d1-b3f8-bd3ea721415d",
                     "text": "Amarteifio, Jessica",
                     "page": "pp. 4",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2023",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_practicing",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Representing on the Schyoty (счёты)\n\nIn *History Tracers*, we will use the abacus as shown by Jessica Amarteifio, as this representation is aligned with the other abacuses we have studied. Thus, when the markers are positioned at the top, the abacus represents the number zero. As we lower the markers toward the bottom, we begin to represent other numbers.\n\nAnalogously, if the abacus were in the vertical position, when the markers were on the right side, we would be representing the number zero. As we moved the markers to the left, we would represent a number.\n\nTo make it clearer, do the following exercise, representing the requested number. By clicking Reset, a new number will be displayed, and you can practice again.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      }
